; The guard: the build gives an error if caravan, caravan.client,
; caravan.websocket, caravan.router or caravan.middleware depends on unix, on
; threads or on a world of weft. Thus the five libraries run in each world.
; weft.linux and weft.kqueue depend on weft.posix, thus the forbidden
; weft.posix also forbids these two worlds.
; weft.os selects a world of the OS, or no world on another system.
; -linkall links each module of the five libraries, thus a module that no
; other module uses also gets the check. nounix.ml is empty. The windtrap
; suites link unix, thus the guard is a separate executable with no test
; library.

(test
 (name nounix)
 (libraries
  caravan
  caravan.client
  caravan.websocket
  caravan.router
  caravan.middleware)
 (link_flags (-linkall))
 (forbidden_libraries unix threads.posix weft.posix weft.sim weft.os))
